 "Hypercalcemia", "Elevated alkaline phosphatase"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "PTH-mediated (Parathyroid) Hypercalcemia", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Classic PTH-mediated hypercalcemia often presents with bone pain. The absence of skeletal symptoms slightly weakens B1 as a consideration."]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Malignancy-associated Hypercalcemia", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.2437589584003247, "posterior": 0.2494633562442696, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Constitutional symptoms and GERD exacerbation are nonspecific but raise suspicion for paraneoplastic syndromes in malignancy. This provides weak support for ma…"], "evidence_against": ["Elevated PTHrP is hallmark of malignancy-associated hypercalcemia. Its absence slightly reduces malignancy's likelihood but doesn't exclude it due to possible …"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.95, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["primary hyperparathyroidism", "humoral hypercalcemia of malignancy", "milk-alkali syndrome", "sarcoidosis"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Vitamin-D / Granulomatous Hypercalcemia", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.06743715134462808, "posterior": 0.06927433649137674, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["No evidence of granulomatous disease (e.g., sarcoidosis) or vitamin D supplementation in the vignette. The absence of these findings weakly argues against vita…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.3, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["primary hyperparathyroidism", "humoral hypercalcemia of malignancy", "milk-alkali syndrome", "sarcoidosis"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Other Hypercalcemic Etiologies (Drug / Endocrine / Immobilization)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.17599928788237185, "posterior": 0.1807940229963068, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Antacid use and low urinary sodium are nonspecific for milk-alkali syndrome. No LR data available for this pattern, but these findings provide minimal support …"], "evidence_against": ["Thiazide diuretics and immobilization are key causes of drug-induced hypercalcemia. Their absence provides weak evidence against B4."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B4.1", "B4.2", "B4.3", "B4.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2.1": {"id": "B2.1", "label": "Humoral Hypercalcemia of Malignancy (PTHrP-mediated)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "B2", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of PTHrP elevation slightly reduces the likelihood of humoral hypercalcemia of malignancy, but constitutional symptoms remain nonspecific and do no…"]}, "B2.2": {"id": "B2.2", "label": "Metastatic Bone Cancer with Lytic Lesions", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.151, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "B2", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Abdominal pain is not typical of metastatic bone cancer, and absence of lytic lesion indicators (glycosylation/macular findings) weakly argues against this mec…"]}, "B2.3": {"id": "B2.3", "label": "Hematologic Malignancy with Hypercalcemia (e.g., Multiple Myeloma, Lymphoma)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.098, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "B2", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of marrow-related findings (anemia, monoclonal protein) weakly argues against hematologic malignancy, though constitutional symptoms maintain some …"]}, "B4.1": {"id": "B4.1", "label": "Milk-Alkali Syndrome (Antacid Overuse)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.073, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "B4", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of antacid overuse documentation and normal renal function weakly argues against milk-alkali syndrome, though antacid use alone remains a potential contri…"]}, "B4.2": {"id": "B4.2", "label": "Hyperthyroidism-induced Hypercalcemia", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.007, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "B4", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of hyperthyroidism-specific findings (tachycardia, tremors) provides moderate evidence against this branch as a cause of hypercalcemia."]}, "B4.3": {"id": "B4.3", "label": "Drug-induced Hypercalcemia (Non-Thiazide Agents)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.058, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "B4", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B4.4": {"id": "B4.4", "label": "Immobilization-related Hypercalcemia", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.043, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "B4", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B3.1": {"id": "B3.1", "label": "Sarcoidosis-induced Hypercalcemia", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.042, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of classic sarcoidosis signs (skin/eye findings) weakly argues against B3.1, though cough remains nonspecific."]}, "B3.2": {"id": "B3.2", "label": "Vitamin D Intoxication", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.019, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["No vitamin D supplementation or intoxication symptoms provides moderate evidence against B3.2, though antacid use remains a potential contributor."]}, "B3.3": {"id": "B3.3", "label": "Other Granulomatous Causes (e.g., Tuberculosis, Histoplasmosis)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.008, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "B3", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of immunocompromised status or travel history weakens but doesn't exclude B3.3 granulomatous infections."]}}, "frontier": [], "other_mass": 0.0, "actions_taken": [{"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of specific granulomatous infection signs (e.g., cough with hemoptysis, night sweats) argue against this branch?", "summary": "Lack of hemoptysis/night sweats slightly reduces probability of granulomatous infections (B3.3) but doesn't confirm exclusion."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of granulomatous disease signs (e.g., skin pigmentation, eye abnormalities) argue against sarcoidosis-induced hypercalcemia?", "summary": "Absence of classic sarcoidosis signs (skin/eye findings) weakly argues against B3.1, though cough remains nonspecific."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the lack of documented vitamin D supplementation or specific intoxication symptoms (e.g., muscle aches, dizziness) argue against this branch?", "summary": "No vitamin D supplementation or intoxication symptoms provides moderate evidence against B3.2, though antacid use remains a potential contributor."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of immunocompromised status or travel history to endemic regions argue against granulomatous infections as a cause?", "summary": "Lack of immunocompromised status or travel history weakens but doesn't exclude B3.3 granulomatous infections."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of a cough without hemoptysis or night sweats (typical granulomatous features) argue against B3.1 sarcoidosis?", "summary": "The absence of typical sarcoidosis features (hemoptysis, night sweats) in a patient with a cough and hypercalcemia provides weak evidence against sarcoidosis-induced hypercalcemia (B3.1), though the cough itself remains nonspecific."}, {"t": 5, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Do the constitutional symptoms (weight loss, trouble focusing) and elevated alkaline phosphatase provide weak support for malignancy as the cause of hypercalcemia over parathyroid or vitamin-D-mediat…", "summary": "The presence of constitutional symptoms (weight loss, trouble focusing) and elevated alkaline phosphatase provides weak support for malignancy as the cause of hypercalcemia, while the absence of specific evidence for parathyroid or vitamin-D-mediated etiologies weakly reduces their likelihood."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B2", 0.2], ["B3", 0.113], ["B4", 0.113]]}, {"top": [["B2", 0.22], ["B4", 0.155], ["B2.2", 0.129]]}, {"top": [["B2", 0.244], ["B4", 0.176], ["B2.2", 0.147]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No universal instability markers present. Hypercalcemia (12.5 mg/dL) is below life-threatening threshold (>14 mg/dL). Vital signs remain stable.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading terminal branch (B2) posterior=0.2198 remains below 0.75 threshold for confirmation. Dangerous alternatives (B2: malignancy, danger=0.9; B4: drug/endocrine, danger=0.7) have posteriors ≥0.10. Info_exhaustion not triggered (estimated_remaining_value=0.55 > 0.10). Further discriminators (PTH testing, imaging) are available and necessary to resolve differential."}, "turn_budget_used": 4, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.4, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.1469421728243714, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the fo